# 6. Recap: Embedded systems

Explain each example aloud before checking the answer.

---

## Follow one signal

Sensor → conversion → decision → display

An enable button is another input.
An actuator changes the environment.
Embedded does not mean Internet-connected.

---

## Count codes correctly

10 bits → 1024 codes: 0–1023.

An ADC code is not automatically a percentage.
PWM changes on-time fraction, not arbitrary smooth voltage.

---

## Calibrate with two references

Dry 800; wet 300.

Raw 550 → relative level 50.
Raw 655 → relative level 29.

Equal references are invalid.

---

## Remember the previous state

Below 30: on. Above 40: off.
30–40 inclusive: keep state. Disabled: off.

**Try:** level 35 from off, then from on.

---

## Timing and evidence matter

A real-time system has a deadline.
Blocking delays can delay input response.

Simulation checks logic.
Physical work must check wiring and calibration.

---

## Explain one sequence

45, 29, 32, 39, 41
→ off, on, on, on, off

**Try:** why does the warning stay on at 39?
Name one thing your simulator did not test.

